.TH ENHANCE-AWEBP 1 "2026-08-07" "enhance-awebp.sh" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
enhance-awebp.sh \- AI upscale animated WebP images with waifu2x
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B enhance-awebp.sh
.P
Takes no arguments. Operates on every
.B .webp
file in the current working directory.
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B enhance-awebp.sh
upscales animated WebP images by dumping their frames, running each frame
through the
.B waifu2x-ncnn-vulkan
neural upscaler, and reassembling the result.
.P
For each
.B .webp
in the current directory:
.IP \(bu 2
The file is checked for animation with
.BR webpinfo (1)
(Chunk VP8X, Animation: 1). Non-animated files are skipped with the message
.B Skipping FILE (not animated).
.IP \(bu 2
The framerate is read with
.BR ffprobe (1)
from the stream's
.B avg_frame_rate
value.
.IP \(bu 2
Frames are extracted with
.BR anim_dump (1)
into a temporary directory.
.IP \(bu 2
Each frame is upscaled with
.B waifu2x-ncnn-vulkan
(
.B \-n 3 \-s 2
).
.IP \(bu 2
The frames are reassembled into
.I basename_enhanced.webp
with
.BR ffmpeg (1)
using
.B \-loop 0
(infinitely looping animation) and the WebP quality below. The temporary
directory is then removed.
.P
Processing messages, including the detected framerate and the output
filename, are printed to standard output.
.SH OPTIONS
None. The script accepts no command line options or arguments; any given
arguments are ignored.
.SH DEFAULTS
Behaviour is controlled by hardcoded defaults at the top of the script:
.TP
.B QUALITY=80
Lossy WebP quality passed to
.B ffmpeg
as
.B \-quality 80
when reassembling the animation.
.TP
.B NOISE=3
Denoise level passed to
.B waifu2x-ncnn-vulkan
as
.B \-n 3
(noise reduction strength).
.TP
.B SCALE=2
Upscaling factor passed to
.B waifu2x-ncnn-vulkan
as
.B \-s 2
(2\(mu magnification).
.P
Changing these values requires editing the script.
.SH EXAMPLES
Run from a directory of animated WebP files:
.IP
.EX
cd ~/Pictures/webp && enhance-awebp.sh
.EE
.P
Resulting files are written next to their source:
.IP
.EX
loop.webp \-> loop_enhanced.webp
.EE
.SH REQUIREMENTS
.IP \(bu 2
.BR webpinfo (1)
.IP \(bu 2
.BR anim_dump (1)
.IP \(bu 2
.BR waifu2x-ncnn-vulkan (1)
.IP \(bu 2
.BR ffmpeg (1)
.IP \(bu 2
.BR ffprobe (1)
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ffmpeg (1),
.BR ffprobe (1)
